# Curriculum catalogue maintenance

When adding or expanding lectures:

1. Create the `.md` under the course `dir` with matching frontmatter (`id`, `prev`/`next`, `manuscript`, `edition`)
2. Register it in `book/curriculum.yaml` (same indentation as siblings)
3. Point the previous lecture’s `next:` at the new id; clear false “end of course” copy
4. Prefer `manuscript: stub` until content exists; flip to `manuscript` when the full lecture lands
5. Regenerate with `python book/tools/curriculum_render.py` and check with `curriculum_validate.py`
6. Optional: `sync_manuscript_meta.py --frontmatter-only` to align frontmatter fields

## Do not

- Hardcode expected lecture counts in tools — the catalogue grows
- Run `curriculum_migrate.py` for brand-new lectures (legacy 60-lecture migration helper)
- Invent course or lecture IDs outside the yaml/manifest scheme
